--------------------------------- KEY POINTS ---------------------------------

✓ Push all opening brackets onto stack
✓ For closing brackets: check if stack empty (underflow)
✓ Match closing with top of stack (LIFO order)
✓ Pop if match found, return false if mismatch
✓ Final check: stack must be empty (all matched)
✓ ArrayDeque is faster than Stack (non-synchronized)

Time: O(n)  |  Space: O(n)  [Stack stores up to n/2 brackets]

//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Parenthesis Checker
Given a string s containing '(', ')', '{', '}', '[', ']', check if it's balanced.

Balanced if:
1. Each opening bracket has a matching closing bracket of same type
2. Brackets are closed in correct order (LIFO)

Examples:
- "[{()}]" → true (all matched correctly)
- "[()()]{}" → true (multiple balanced groups)
- "([]" → false (missing ')')
- "([{]})" → false (wrong order)

Constraints:
- 1 ≤ s.size() ≤ 10⁶
- s[i] ∈ {'{', '}', '(', ')', '[', ']'}

Your Approach: Stack-based matching
- Push opening brackets
- For closing: match with top, pop if valid
- Return true if stack empty at end

Time: O(n) | Space: O(n)
